From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: shell32: a standard user's shell folders resolve (read-only profile list)

On the shared system prefix only administrators may write HKLM. shell32
opened HKLM\...\ProfileList with KEY_ALL_ACCESS (creating it) merely to read
the profiles directory; for a standard user that failed, so
_SHExpandEnvironmentStrings expanded nothing and returned an empty string --
which _SHGetUserShellFolderPath then wrote into the user's "Shell Folders"
cache. From then on SHGetFolderPath(CSIDL_DESKTOPDIRECTORY) failed:
ShellExecute of a shortcut reported "file not found" and explorer showed no
desktop icons.

- The profile list is opened read-only when it cannot be opened for writing,
  and without it (not even readable) Windows' defaults are used; a default
  is the answer whether or not it could be saved.
- A path that did not expand is never cached: the lookup fails instead of
  poisoning "Shell Folders". A cache that cannot be written does not fail a
  lookup whose path is right.

Gate: test/shellfolders-gate.sh -- the profile list read-only for users,
the Desktop asked for with Administrators disabled.
---
--- a/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
@@ -2154,15 +2154,22 @@
